===BODY===
          <h2>A long way from home</h2>
          <p>From Málaga or Alicante, the drive back to the UK is well over 2,000 km. When a car breaks down that far away, getting it repaired locally can take a long time, especially for parts or bodywork. That's when many people choose to have the car brought home and repaired by a garage they know.</p>

          <h2>Where we collect from</h2>
          <p>We collect from all over Spain: the Costa del Sol (Málaga, Marbella), the Costa Blanca (Alicante, Benidorm), Murcia, Valencia, Barcelona and the Costa Brava, Madrid, and the north coast around Santander and Bilbao. Cars stored at a garage, a pound, a holiday home or a car park are all fine, as long as someone can give access.</p>

          <h2>How the car comes back</h2>
          <p>Depending on where the car is and the timing, it either travels north through France to the Channel or comes back on one of the long ferry routes from northern Spain to the south coast of England. We'll pick the most sensible option and include it in a fixed price for the whole journey.</p>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Leaving the car behind?</strong> Give the keys and a signed note to the garage or a neighbour, take photos of the car, and send us the exact address. That's all we need to collect it after you've flown home.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Insurance</h2>
          <p>Check whether your European breakdown cover includes repatriation. Many policies do if repairs would take more than a few days. If you need to arrange it yourself, we'll give you a written quote you can send to your insurer.</p>
===FAQ===
Q: Can you collect a car from a holiday home in Spain?
A: Yes, as long as someone can give access and hand over the keys, or the keys are left with a neighbour or the garage. Send us the exact address and a contact.
Q: How long does it take to bring a car back from Spain?
A: It's a long journey, and timing depends on the location and the crossing used. We'll tell you the expected collection and delivery times when we quote.
Q: Can you bring back a car that doesn't run?
A: Yes. Non-runners and accident-damaged cars are fine. Just tell us when you ask for a quote, so it's loaded with the right equipment.
